{"case_id":"T8023","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["configuration","input semantics","attack surface"],"commit_induced":"YES","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":98,"affected_functions":["parseAndPrintFile","xmllintShell","xmllintMain"],"reason":"S1 removes the XMLLINT_FUZZ exclusion around the lint->shell branch in parseAndPrintFile, making interactive xmllintShell behavior part of the fuzz build's production surface. H0 cannot exercise it because its switches array does not contain \"--shell\", and H0 provides fuzz-controlled document resources but no fuzz-controlled interactive shell input. This gap did not exist in S0 + H0 because the entire shell branch was compiled out under XMLLINT_FUZZ.","evidence":["H0 defines XMLLINT_FUZZ before including ../xmllint.c.","S0 guarded the lint->shell call to xmllintShell(doc, filename, stdout) with #ifndef XMLLINT_FUZZ; S1 removes that guard.","H0's switches array includes many xmllint options but not \"--shell\", so its generated argv cannot select lint->shell.","The newly added private/lint.h declares xmllintShell and xmllintMain, while xmllintMain becoming non-static and moving main to lintmain.c otherwise preserves H0's existing direct xmllintMain invocation."],"recommended_action":"Extend H0 with a fuzz-safe shell mode that can select \"--shell\" and supplies bounded, fuzz-controlled shell commands through the expected input channel, with per-input state cleanup; alternatively keep shell interaction explicitly excluded from this harness and cover xmllintShell with a dedicated target."}
